@startuml
title RustServer.Auth — administrator actions and provider linking

hide footbox
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 82

actor Browser
participant "AdminPortalController\n/admin" as AdminPortal
participant "Razor page\nSERVER ACCESS" as AdminPage
participant "Identity / authorization" as Identity
participant "CSRF endpoint\n/api/auth/csrf" as Antiforgery
participant "LogoutController\n/api/auth/logout" as Logout
participant "Google link controller\n/api/auth/google/link" as GoogleLink
participant "Google middleware\n/signin-google" as GoogleMiddleware
participant "Steam link controller\n/api/auth/steam/link" as SteamLink
participant "Steam middleware\n/signin-steam" as SteamMiddleware
participant "Other platform applications\n/player, /dashboard" as Applications
database "Identity data store" as Store

note over AdminPortal, Applications
  RustServer.Auth owns /admin and all /api/auth/* routes.
  /player and /dashboard belong to other platform applications;
  Auth renders links to them but does not implement them.
end note

== Open the administrator portal ==

Browser -> AdminPortal: GET /admin
AdminPortal -> Identity: Get current user and verify Admin role
alt Administrator
  Identity -> Store: Read user, roles and linked providers
  Store --> Identity: Access allowed
  Identity --> AdminPortal: true
  AdminPortal --> Browser: 200 OK — SERVER ACCESS page
  Browser -> AdminPage: Run inline JavaScript
  AdminPage -> Identity: GET /api/auth/me
  Identity --> AdminPage: 200 OK — current user and link status
else Anonymous or non-Admin user
  Identity --> AdminPortal: false
  AdminPortal --> Browser: 404 Not Found
  note right of AdminPortal
    If the page's /api/auth/me call is unauthenticated,
    its JavaScript navigates to /login.
  end note
end

== Action 1 — Player Portal ==

AdminPage -> Browser: Navigate through href="/player"
Browser -> Applications: GET /player

== Action 2 — Admin Dashboard ==

AdminPage -> Browser: Navigate through href="/dashboard"
Browser -> Applications: GET /dashboard

== Action 3 — Sign Out ==

AdminPage -> Antiforgery: GET /api/auth/csrf
Antiforgery --> AdminPage: 200 OK — { token }
AdminPage -> Logout: POST /api/auth/logout\nX-CSRF-TOKEN + auth cookie
alt Authenticated request with valid CSRF token
  Logout -> Identity: SignOutAsync()
  Identity --> Logout: Clear RustServer.Auth cookie
  Logout --> AdminPage: 204 No Content
  AdminPage -> Browser: window.location.replace('/login')
else Missing session or invalid CSRF token
  Logout --> AdminPage: 401 Unauthorized or 400 Bad Request
  AdminPage -> Browser: Display sign-out error
end

== Action 4 — Link Google ==

Browser -> GoogleLink: GET /api/auth/google/link
GoogleLink -> Identity: Create challenge with application callback\n/api/auth/google/link-callback and user ID
GoogleLink -> GoogleMiddleware: Challenge("Google")
GoogleMiddleware --> Browser: 302 Google authorization endpoint
Browser -> GoogleMiddleware: GET /signin-google after Google authorization
GoogleMiddleware --> Browser: 302 application callback
Browser -> GoogleLink: GET /api/auth/google/link-callback
GoogleLink -> Identity: Validate ownership and persist external login
alt Link succeeds or already belongs to this user
  GoogleLink --> Browser: 302 Location: /admin?googleLinked=1
else Link fails
  GoogleLink --> Browser: 400 Bad Request
end

== Action 5 — Link Steam ==

Browser -> SteamLink: GET /api/auth/steam/link
SteamLink -> Identity: Create challenge with application callback\n/api/auth/steam/link-callback and user ID
SteamLink -> SteamMiddleware: Challenge("Steam")
SteamMiddleware --> Browser: 302 Steam OpenID endpoint
Browser -> SteamMiddleware: GET /signin-steam after Steam verification
SteamMiddleware --> Browser: 302 application callback
Browser -> SteamLink: GET /api/auth/steam/link-callback
SteamLink -> Identity: Validate ownership and persist external login
alt Link succeeds or already belongs to this user
  SteamLink --> Browser: 302 Location: /admin?steamLinked=1
else Link fails
  SteamLink --> Browser: 400 Bad Request
end

@enduml
